# PROBE different-individuals. a ≠ b with A ⊑ {a} and A ⊑ {b} makes A unsatisfiable, and the ontology stays consistent.
# construct: DifferentIndividuals
# expect: unsat :A
# expect-not: inconsistent

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual . :b a owl:NamedIndividual .
:a owl:differentFrom :b .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Class ; owl:oneOf ( :a ) ] .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Class ; owl:oneOf ( :b ) ] .
